What:           /sys/fs/btrfs/<uuid>/qgroups/remove_after_rescan_fallback
Date:           2026-10-20
Contact:        linux-btrfs@vger.kernel.org
Description:
                Controls whether a qgroup is removed from the in-memory tree
                after relation removal requests a qgroup rescan. The value is
                a boolean and defaults to 1. When set to 0, qgroup removal
                returns immediately on the rescan request, matching the
                original behavior before the cleanup fix.

                Disabling this fix can leave a qgroup in memory after its
                on-disk info item has been deleted, causing later qgroup
                accounting to report a missing info item. Use 0 only for
                isolated diagnostic workloads. Changing the value affects
                future qgroup removals and does not repair existing state.
